From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:45:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add host defaults for new agents and worktrees

A host owner could not set how new agents and worktrees start on every
client. Two host settings now cover that, each with its own feature flag.

Default mode per provider: new agents took their mode from whatever each
device last remembered. The host config now stores an optional
defaultModeId per provider (agents.providers.<id>.defaultModeId), editable
through the mutable daemon config; null clears it. When the mode still
exists in the provider's catalog, the daemon reports it as the provider's
defaultModeId (so clients with nothing remembered use it) plus a new
hostDefaultModeId snapshot field, and uses it for top-level, attended
creates that omit a mode. Parent inheritance, unattended selection and
explicit modes are unchanged, and a stale id falls back to the provider's
own default. The app gates on server_info.features.providerDefaultMode:
Host settings > Agents gets a per-provider picker, and agent form
resolution lets a host default beat the per-device remembered mode while
explicit initial modes still win.

Default worktree setup: projects without a worktree.setup in paseo.json
got no setup in new worktrees. The host config now stores optional default
setup commands (worktrees.defaultSetup in config.json), exposed as
worktreeDefaultSetup in the mutable daemon config; null clears them.
Worktree setup resolution falls back to these commands only when the
project's paseo.json leaves worktree.setup out entirely. The normalized
config turns an absent and an empty setup into the same [], so the raw
config decides; a project that declares any setup, even an empty one,
keeps its own. The fallback sits in getWorktreeSetupCommands, so worktree
creation and bootstrap both get it. The app gates on
server_info.features.worktreeDefaultSetup: Host settings > Workspaces gets
a one-command-per-line editor, and a project's setup field says when the
host default applies.

Fork-Change: F-3
